%N A398757 a(n) = A401692(n) - 10^(n-1), the distance between A401692(n) and the smallest n-digit number.
%H A398757 Jean-Marc Rebert, <a href="/A398757/a398757.txt">n, a(n), and two largest prime factors of 10^(n-1) + a(n)</a>.
%e A398757 a(3) = A401692(3) - 10^(3-1) = 102 - 100 = 2.
%o A398757 (PARI) isok(k) = my(f=factor(k)[, 1]~, i=#f); if (i>1, #Str(f[i]) == 1 + #Str(f[i-1]));
%o A398757 a(n) = my(k=10^(n-1)); while(!isok(k), k++); k-10^(n-1); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Nov 03 2026
